\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.2}{\ignorespaces \footnotesize  (a) execution graph of MP-trans violating $\mathsf  {WRA}$ : we have $\mathtt  {w}(x,0)\nobreakspace  {}\mathsf  {\color  {colorHB}hb}\nobreakspace  {}\mathtt  {w}(x,1)\nobreakspace  {}\mathsf  {\color  {colorHB}hb}\nobreakspace  {}\mathtt  {r}(x,0)\nobreakspace  {}\mathsf  {\color  {colorRF}rf}^{-1}\nobreakspace  {}\mathtt  {w}(x,0)$ which violates weak-read-coherence. (b) execution graph of WWrace consistent with $\mathsf  {WRA}$ but violating $\mathsf  {RA}$ : we have $\mathtt  {r}(x,1)\nobreakspace  {}\mathsf  {\color  {colorRF}rf}^{-1}\mathtt  {w}(x,1)\nobreakspace  {}\mathsf  {\color  {colorMO}mo}\nobreakspace  {}\mathtt  {w}(x,2)\nobreakspace  {}\mathsf  {\color  {colorHB}hb}\nobreakspace  {}\mathtt  {r}(x,1)$ violating read coherence. (c) execution graph of 2+2W which is $\mathsf  {RA}$ consistent but violating $\mathsf  {SRA}$ : we have $\mathtt  {w}(x,1)\nobreakspace  {}\mathsf  {\color  {colorHB}hb}\nobreakspace  {}\mathtt  {w}(y,2)\nobreakspace  {}\mathsf  {\color  {colorMO}mo}\nobreakspace  {}\mathtt  {w}(y,1)\nobreakspace  {}\mathsf  {\color  {colorHB}hb}\nobreakspace  {}\mathtt  {w}(x,2)\nobreakspace  {}\mathsf  {\color  {colorMO}mo}\nobreakspace  {}\mathtt  {w}(x,1)$ violating strong-write-coherence. (d) execution graph of Jumping which is $\mathsf  {SRA}$ consistent, but violates $\mathsf  {SC}$: we have $\mathtt  {w}(x,1)\nobreakspace  {}\mathsf  {\color  {colorPO}po}\nobreakspace  {}\mathtt  {w}(y,1)\nobreakspace  {}\mathsf  {\color  {colorRF}rf}\nobreakspace  {}\mathtt  {r}(y,1)\nobreakspace  {}\mathsf  {\color  {colorPO}po}\nobreakspace  {}\mathtt  {r}(x,2)\nobreakspace  {}\mathsf  {\color  {colorFR}fr}\nobreakspace  {}\mathtt  {w}(x,1)$ violating $\mathsf  {acy}(\mathsf  {\color  {colorPO}po}\cup \mathsf  {\color  {colorRF}rf}\cup \mathsf  {\color  {colorMO}mo}\cup \mathsf  {\color  {colorFR}fr})$. \relax }}{31}{figure.caption.37}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{examplesra}{{5.2}{31}{\footnotesize (a) execution graph of MP-trans violating $\wramm $ : we have $\wt (x,0)~\hb ~\wt (x,1)~\hb ~\rd (x,0)~\rf ^{-1}~\wt (x,0)$ which violates weak-read-coherence. (b) execution graph of WWrace consistent with $\wramm $ but violating $\ramm $ : we have $\rd (x,1)~\rf ^{-1}\wt (x,1)~\mo ~\wt (x,2)~\hb ~\rd (x,1)$ violating read coherence. (c) execution graph of 2+2W which is $\ramm $ consistent but violating $\sramm $ : we have $\wt (x,1)~\hb ~\wt (y,2)~\mo ~\wt (y,1)~\hb ~\wt (x,2)~\mo ~\wt (x,1)$ violating strong-write-coherence. (d) execution graph of Jumping which is $\sramm $ consistent, but violates $\scmm $: we have $\wt (x,1)~\po ~\wt (y,1)~\rf ~\rd (y,1)~\po ~\rd (x,2)~\fr ~\wt (x,1)$ violating $\acy (\po \cup \rf \cup \mo \cup \fr )$. \relax }{figure.caption.37}{}}
