\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces \footnotesize  From left: $\mathsf  {\color  {colorRF}rf}_0 \sqsubseteq \mathsf  {\color  {colorRF}rf}_1 \sqsubseteq \mathsf  {\color  {colorRF}rf}_2$. $\mathsf  {\color  {colorRF}rf}_0$ has a violation of weak-read-coherence{}:\nobreakspace  {}$\mathtt  {r}_3 \xrightarrow {\mathsf  {\color  {colorRF}rf}_{0}^{-1}} \mathtt  {w}_1 \xrightarrow {\mathsf  {\color  {colorPO}po}} \mathtt  {w}_2 \xrightarrow {\mathsf  {\color  {colorHB}hb}_0} \mathtt  {r}_3 $. $\mathsf  {\color  {colorRF}rf}_1$ has a violation of weak-read-coherence{}:\nobreakspace  {}$\mathtt  {r}_4 \xrightarrow {\mathsf  {\color  {colorRF}rf}_{1}^{-1}} \mathtt  {w}_2 \xrightarrow {\mathsf  {\color  {colorPO}po}} \mathtt  {w}_3 \xrightarrow {\mathsf  {\color  {colorHB}hb}_1} \mathtt  {r}_4 $. $\mathsf  {\color  {colorRF}rf}_2$ does not have any more violations of weak-read-coherence{}. porf-acyclicity{} is also satisfied by $\mathsf  {\color  {colorRF}rf}_2$. The underlying partial execution graph is $\mathsf  {WRA}$-consistent. \relax }}{37}{figure.caption.40}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{Example-one-writer-without-porfcycle}{{6.1}{37}{\footnotesize From left: $\rf _0 \sqsubseteq \rf _1 \sqsubseteq \rf _2$. $\rf _0$ has a violation of \WRCoh {}:~$\rd _3 \xra {\rf _{0}^{-1}} \wt _1 \xra {\po } \wt _2 \xra {\hb _0} \rd _3 $. $\rf _1$ has a violation of \WRCoh {}:~$\rd _4 \xra {\rf _{1}^{-1}} \wt _2 \xra {\po } \wt _3 \xra {\hb _1} \rd _4 $. $\rf _2$ does not have any more violations of \WRCoh {}. \PORF {} is also satisfied by $\rf _2$. The underlying partial execution graph is $\wramm $-consistent. \relax }{figure.caption.40}{}}
