\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.2}{\ignorespaces \footnotesize  From left: $\mathsf  {\color  {colorRF}rf}_0 \sqsubseteq \mathsf  {\color  {colorRF}rf}_1$. $\mathsf  {\color  {colorRF}rf}_0$ has a violation of weak-read-coherence{}:\nobreakspace  {}$\mathtt  {r}_3 \xrightarrow {\mathsf  {\color  {colorRF}rf}_{0}^{-1}} \mathtt  {w}_1 \xrightarrow {\mathsf  {\color  {colorPO}po}} \mathtt  {w}_2 \xrightarrow {\mathsf  {\color  {colorHB}hb}} \mathtt  {r}_3 $. $\mathsf  {\color  {colorRF}rf}_1$ has no weak-read-coherence{} violation but does not satisfy porf-acyclicity{}:\nobreakspace  {}$\mathtt  {w}_5 \xrightarrow {\mathsf  {\color  {colorRF}rf}_{1}} \mathtt  {r}_3 \xrightarrow {\mathsf  {\color  {colorPO}po}} \mathtt  {w}_4 \xrightarrow {\mathsf  {\color  {colorRF}rf}} \mathtt  {r}_2 \xrightarrow {\mathsf  {\color  {colorPO}po}} \mathtt  {w}_5$. The partial execution graph is not $\mathsf  {WRA}$-consistent. \relax }}{37}{figure.caption.41}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{Example-one-writer-with-porfcycle}{{6.2}{37}{\footnotesize From left: $\rf _0 \sqsubseteq \rf _1$. $\rf _0$ has a violation of \WRCoh {}:~$\rd _3 \xra {\rf _{0}^{-1}} \wt _1 \xra {\po } \wt _2 \xra {\hb } \rd _3 $. $\rf _1$ has no \WRCoh {} violation but does not satisfy \PORF {}:~$\wt _5 \xra {\rf _{1}} \rd _3 \xra {\po } \wt _4 \xra {\rf } \rd _2 \xra {\po } \wt _5$. The partial execution graph is not $\wramm $-consistent. \relax }{figure.caption.41}{}}
